arguments.prompt:
You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a recipe sharing community. The project has been scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-254e7e4735914033bbe8f457202683cd/RecipeShare` using `dotnet new blazor -int Server` (per-page interactivity).

## What exists now
- Standard Blazor template with Counter.razor, Weather.razor, Home.razor, Error.razor, NotFound.razor
- NavMenu.razor with links to Home, Counter, Weather
- MainLayout.razor with sidebar + content area
- Program.cs with `AddRazorComponents().AddInteractiveServerComponents()` and `MapRazorComponents<App>().AddInteractiveServerRenderMode()`
- _Imports.razor with standard usings including `@using static Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web.RenderMode`

## Requirements
1. Browse recipes by category — read-only content pages (static SSR)
2. Each recipe page has a star-rating widget (click to rate 1–5 stars) — needs `@rendermode InteractiveServer`
3. A "Submit Recipe" page with a form (title, ingredients, steps) — needs `@rendermode InteractiveServer`
4. Homepage displays recipe categories (static content)
5. Most pages are read-only; only the rating widget and submit form need interactivity

## Tasks

### 1. Delete template pages
Delete these files:
- `Components/Pages/Counter.razor`
- `Components/Pages/Weather.razor`

### 2. Create a data model and service
Create `Models/Recipe.cs` with:
```csharp
namespace RecipeShare.Models;

public class Recipe
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Title { get; set; } = "";
    public string Category { get; set; } = "";
    public string Description { get; set; } = "";
    public List<string> Ingredients { get; set; } = new();
    public List<string> Steps { get; set; } = new();
    public int TotalRatings { get; set; }
    public int RatingSum { get; set; }
    public double AverageRating => TotalRatings > 0 ? (double)RatingSum / TotalRatings : 0;
}
```

