### 3. Register the service in Program.cs
Add `using RecipeShare.Services;` and `builder.Services.AddSingleton<RecipeService>();` before `var app = ...`.

### 4. Update _Imports.razor
Add:
```
@using RecipeShare.Models
@using RecipeShare.Services
```

### 5. Create StarRating component
Create `Components/StarRating.razor` — this is an interactive component:
```razor
@rendermode InteractiveServer

<div class="star-rating">
    @for (int i = 1; i <= 5; i++)
    {
        var star = i;
        <span class="star @(star <= _selectedRating ? "filled" : "")"
              @onclick="() => Rate(star)"
              role="button"
              title="@star star(s)">
            @(star <= _selectedRating ? "★" : "☆")
        </span>
    }
    @if (_hasRated)
    {
        <span class="ms-2 text-success">Thanks for rating!</span>
    }
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public int RecipeId { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<int> OnRated { get; set; }

    [Inject] private RecipeService RecipeService { get; set; } = default!;

    private int _selectedRating;
    private bool _hasRated;

    private async Task Rate(int stars)
    {
        if (_hasRated) return;
        _selectedRating = stars;
        _hasRated = true;
        RecipeService.AddRating(RecipeId, stars);
        await OnRated.InvokeAsync(stars);
    }
}
```

Create `Components/StarRating.razor.css`:
